.DS_Store
*.pyc
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.env
.venv
venv/
env/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
dist/
build/
*.log
node_modules/

# Build artifacts from `az bicep build`: the .bicep files are the source of truth
infra/*.json

# Local agent settings (machine-specific, may contain credentials)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Downloaded extension catalog cache: refetched on demand, not source of truth
.specify/extensions/.cache/

# Spec Kit workflow state: local progress tracking, not source of truth
specs/**/.spec-context.json

# Command output captured while verifying a feature against a live subscription.
# Evidence of a run, not a source of truth: findings that matter are written
# into the spec artifacts and the deployment runbook instead.
specs/**/evidence/

# Generated dataset and downloaded model artifact for feature 005. Both are
# build outputs: the CSV is reproducible from generate_data.py and its seed, and
# the model is retrievable from the run that produced it. The scripts are the
# source of truth, the bytes are not.
mlops/training-pipeline/data/
mlops/training-pipeline/downloaded-model/

# Model copies fetched from the workspace, and the artifacts derived from them.
# All retrievable: registered-model/ is whatever the registry resolves for a
# given version, serving-model/ is that plus a one-line conda edit recorded in
# results.md, and the scoring input and its predictions are regenerated by
# make_scoring_input.py from the same pinned seed.
mlops/training-pipeline/registered-model/
mlops/training-pipeline/serving-model/
mlops/training-pipeline/scoring-input/
mlops/training-pipeline/registered-predictions.json

# MLflow's local fallback store. It appears whenever a script calls into MLflow
# without an azureml-backed tracking URI - which is precisely the failure mode
# train.py refuses to train under. Never a deliverable, and on a compute node it
# is what silently swallows a run's metrics before the node is released.
mlruns/

# The recorded baseline. Evidence of a measurement, not a source of truth - the
# same reasoning that keeps specs/**/evidence/ out. Its values are written into
# the feature's results.md, and generate_data.py and baseline.py reproduce the
# file byte for byte from the pinned seed, so a clone rebuilds it rather than
# inheriting it.
mlops/training-pipeline/baseline.json

# Retrieval runs for feature 008. Regenerable by command from the index, at the
# cost of one query embedding each. The label set beside them is the opposite -
# no command reproduces a human judgment - so questions/ stays tracked.
rag-optimization/rag-block5/runs/

# The cut corpus. A build output of chunk_corpus.py over docs/exam-notes at a
# commit, and every chunk carries that commit - so the pair (script, commit)
# reproduces it byte for byte. Tracking it would be tracking the same text twice.
rag-optimization/rag-block5/chunks.jsonl

# Personal study material: exam notes, flashcards, progress tracker.
# Kept out of the repo deliberately - see the "*.local.md" convention.
*.local.md
